{{also|pondérable}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|ponder|able}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{senseid|en|physics}}{{lb|en|physics}} Having a detectable amount of matter; having a measurable [[mass]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1910|author=E. T. Whittaker|title=A History of the Theories of Aether and Electricity|page=35|publisher=Dublin University Press|year_published=1910
|passage=[T]he imponderability of heat did not appear to the philosophers of the eighteenth century to be a sufficient reason for excluding it from the list of chemical elements; and... there was... doubt... whether [[caloric#English:_Obsolete_heat|caloric]] was '''ponderable''' or not.}}
# Worthy of note; [[significant]], [[interesting]].
# {{lb|en|rare}} [[heavy|Heavy]]; [[ponderous]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1936|author=Djuna Barnes|title=Nightwood|page=77|publisher=Faber & Faber|year_published=2007
|passage=The very mother's head you swore by in the dock is a heavier head, crowned with '''ponderable''' hair.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|having mass}} {{l|en|massive}}
* {{sense|worthy of note}} {{l|en|eminent}}, {{l|en|noteworthy}}; see also [[Thesaurus:notable]]
* {{sense|heavy, ponderous}} {{l|en|hefty}}, {{l|en|massive}}, {{l|en|weighty}}

